From fc6581b2e680d7e509c9eb319a5c87c7df769db3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sebastian Wick <sebastian.wick@redhat.com>
Date: Fri, 19 Jun 2026 18:38:41 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 01/16] context: Make dispatching DBus interface skeletons in
 threads explicit

We're going to add dispatching in fibers as well, and we want to replace
the threads with it, so a default to threads is not desired anymore.

This also changes the XDP_CONTEXT_EXPORT_FLAGS_HOST_PORTAL flag which so
far meant "run on the main thread and don't authenticate". Now that the
default flags mean "run on the main thread" we can drop the host portal
flag and instead add XDP_CONTEXT_EXPORT_FLAGS_SKIP_AUTH to skip
authentication.


NOTE (SUSE): We backported this patch and adjusted the paths of the
             source files, since in 1.22, every file is located under src/
Refreshed for 1.22.1 (fuzz-free).
